+# Plan 007: 33-dev pass rate (pre-registered 2026-11-06T07:10Z, BEFORE any plan-007 run; dec 058 item 7, dec 061 item 4, dec 062 items 4-5)
+Supersedes the earlier "time-aware budget lever" draft (kept verbatim as Appendix Z, not scheduled).
+
+## Question
+We have zero local pass-rate numbers. Arm 1 measures the exact pass/fail of the current default 31B config (thinking off) on all
+33 dev tasks. Arm 2 (next week) is the paired thinking-on vs thinking-off comparison that the n=8 empty-diff screens cannot answer.
+
+## Arms
+- ARM 1 (now, expiring quota): bundle 31b-v009-p7a1 = bundles/31b/v009 = dist/31b-v009.zip sha256=d38c55c79103950d6d269a722bd0c9db9db22e1c0ec96be230f6c24a332d130d
+  = 31b-v006-p5d (plan 005 arm D: thinking_budget 0, plan-005 arm-B prompt, no repo-named hint) with ONLY max_time_minutes 4.0 -> 3.5
+  (= the 31b-v002 cap, the FINALS-RULE maximum if v002 scores). Root T 0.2, analyzer T 0.2 + own thinking_budget 4096, 40 calls/50 turns,
+  max_output_tokens 8192 x2. Choice rationale: thinking off is the current default direction (dec 059 item 1); 3.5 is the only cap that
+  matters if 31b-v002 scores, which dec 061 (i) makes the next 31B question. A cap-1.23 pass rate is NOT measured here (CAP-BOUND, report 014).
+- ARM 2 (after the 2026-11-07 reset; NOT run before then): v009 with ONLY root thinking_budget 0 -> 4096 (= v002 thinking setting), all else equal.
+  Same ids, same order, same kernel code, k=1. Packed and reviewed before it runs.
+
+## Environment (dec 034 item 6 / dec 058 item 7: which env the local sandbox models, and why)
+Docker-path emulation of Dockerfile.public (dec 027, the plan-006 kernel stack, setup_fix=1): editable install + test deps from the
+offline /wheels via the harness setup.py into the sandbox venv; verification = the stock swegemma verify_task (Container B: fresh
+sandbox, agent patch with test/config files stripped, hidden test_patch applied, pytest on the target test files, resolved = exit 0).
+Why this env and not H1 (test deps from the scorer notebook's site-packages): (1) the clean list (48) and dev split were calibrated
+with gold and null patches in this same docker-path emulation (results/gold_calibration_per_task.jsonl), so "dev task is solvable"
+is only defined here; (2) no H1 gold calibration exists, so an H1 pass rate could not separate agent failures from env failures;
+(3) the agent-side env is the same one all plan-005/006 screens used. Known gap: if the scorer runs H1, some tasks may pass or fail
+differently from the scorer for env reasons (sign unknown). Follow-up, not part of this plan's runs: a CPU-only Kaggle gold+null pass
+of the 33 dev ids through the same kernel verification path (and, separately, an H1 variant) to measure the env-disagreement rate.
+
+## Protocol
+- Ids: all 33 of eval/splits/dev.txt (sha256 bff0841a...d2d7), run in the fixed pre-registered order eval/plans/007-arm1-ids.txt
+  (sorted by sha256("plan007:"+id); file sha256 69fc5b32...e930). The order makes any completed prefix a random subset.
+- Kernel: eval/kaggle/timing_push.sh --with-verification --no-stock-probe aniket0202/gemma-31b-passrate bundles/31b/v009 <ids> <budget>.
+  The only kernel-stack change vs arm F (b4d9f59) is the --no-stock-probe push flag (STOCK_PROBE=False skips the plan-006 P1
+  stock-setup timing probe, ~120 s/task, which affects no agent or verification step). Conc 1, 4x L4, k=1. Quality run: this is
+  not a timing measurement (wall times are recorded, descriptive only).
+- SMOKE first: the first 3 ids (eval/plans/007-smoke-ids.txt: 2 rich + 1 fastapi), budget 4800 s. Smoke gate (all must hold):
+  3/3 rows present with no harness/row error, no setup_failed/editable_failed, verification exit code in {0,1} for every task
+  (2/4/5/None = verification env problem), vLLM up. If it holds AND no code/bundle byte changes before the main push, the 3 smoke
+  rows COUNT as arm-1 rows and the main kernel runs ids 4..33. If any code or bundle byte changes, smoke rows are discarded and all
+  33 rerun. Smoke gate FAIL: no main run today; diagnose, and the run moves after the reset (dec 062 item 4: no rushing).
+- Chunking: the main kernel gets KERNEL_BUDGET sized from the smoke per-task wall and the quota left before the reset (target: total
+  week usage <= 29.5/30 h). The kernel stops starting new tasks near the budget; unrun ids (a suffix of the fixed order) run as chunk 2
+  after the reset with identical bundle and code. Arm 1 is reported only when all 33 ids have a row (a prefix-only interim may be
+  reported, clearly labelled, with n).
+- Quota logged before/after every kernel in ops/budget/kaggle.md. No GCP spend. Never delays the dec 055 checklist at 2026-11-07T00:00Z.
+
+## Metrics
+- PRIMARY: resolved count / 33 (exact harness verdict), Wilson 95% CI. Harness errors (verification exit not in {0,1}, row errors,
+  setup failures) count as FAIL in the primary and are listed separately; sensitivity line = pass rate over tasks without harness error.
+- Per repo (rich 27, fastapi 6), descriptive. Note: dev includes the 8 plan-005/006 screen ids (tuned-on); report pass rate on the 25
+  never-screened ids separately as a descriptive line.
+- Secondary (descriptive): empty-patch count, timeouts, submit_patch called, test files edited, stray files, agent wall p50/p90,
+  verification wall p50/p90, LLM calls/tool calls per task.
+- Dec 060 Addendum metric (all arms): identical consecutive tool-call runs (same tool + byte-identical args): per-task max run,
+  tasks with run >= 3 and >= 5, total repeated calls (code: eval/plan005_armF_compare.py logic).
+- Dec 062 item 5: thinking blocks per task (count + total chars; eval/thinking_bound.py logic), descriptive; with thinking_budget 0
+  one 17-char block was seen in arm F.
+
+## Decision rules
+- ARM 1 alone is a measurement: no ship decision follows from it. It sets the baseline for arm 2 and is cited in the dec 061 (i)
+  v004 cap discussion. If the primary is 0/33 with harness errors on >= 5 tasks, arm 1 is INVALID (env problem), not a quality result.
+- ARM 2 vs ARM 1 (paired, same 33 ids, k=1): discordant counts on-only / off-only, exact two-sided sign test.
+  Adopt thinking ON if on-only > off-only with p < 0.2 AND on has no more timeouts than off + 2 AND a cap-3.5 timing check passes;
+  adopt OFF (keep default) if off-only >= on-only; otherwise (on ahead, p >= 0.2) NO-DIFFERENCE: keep OFF (cheaper, faster), and k=2
+  for both arms only if quota allows (a second seed per arm, same rule on the pooled pairs). +-3 tasks on 33 is noise.
+- Cost note: verification adds a fresh sandbox setup per task (Container B, two dependency installs), so per-task wall is higher than
+  the plan-005 screens (~5.5 min/task); the smoke measures it. If arm 2 at k=1 does not fit next week's quota with other approved work,
+  the arm-2 schedule comes back to the Director with the measured numbers.
+
+## Repeat guard (dec 062 item 3)
+CPU-only design note delivered as eval/plans/007-repeat-guard.md (by 2026-11-07T18:00Z). Not built, not packed.
+
